:Namespace Kafka
⍝ A small, friendly layer over Dyalog's Kafka interface (vendor/, v0.1.117).
⍝ Runs in the dyalog-kafka image (see ../Dockerfile).
⍝
⍝   Kafka.Init                                   ⍝ load the library (once)
⍝   p←Kafka.Producer 'apl-kafka:19092'
⍝   p Kafka.Send 'orders' order 'North'          ⍝ topic value [key]
⍝   Kafka.Flush p                                ⍝ wait for delivery
⍝   c←Kafka.Consumer 'apl-kafka:19092' 'my-group' 'orders'
⍝   msgs←Kafka.Poll c                            ⍝ messages as namespaces
⍝   msgs.(key value offset)   msgs.data          ⍝ data: the value parsed as JSON
⍝
⍝ Values: text is sent as is; anything else (numbers, arrays, namespaces)
⍝ is sent as JSON. Everything is UTF-8 encoded, so 'Zoë ⍳⍴' survives.

    ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1
    Lib←'/opt/dyalog-kafka'         ⍝ where the Dockerfile puts kafka.so

    ∇ Init;home;src;names;types
    ⍝ Load Dyalog's Kafka APL source into # and the shared library.
    ⍝ DYALOG_KAFKA_HOME is this integration's folder (default: in the repo at /app).
      :If 0≠⎕NC'⍙ready' ⋄ :Return ⋄ :EndIf
      home←{0=≢⍵:'/app/integrations/kafka' ⋄ ⍵}2⎕NQ'.' 'GetEnvironment' 'DYALOG_KAFKA_HOME'
      src←home,'/vendor/aplsource/'
      #.kafka←#.⎕NS''
      (names types)←0 1(⎕NINFO⍠1)src,'kafka/*.aplf'
      {}{2 #.kafka.⎕FIX'file://',⍵}¨names
      {}2 #.⎕FIX'file://',src,'Init.aplf'
      {}{#.⎕FIX'file://',src,⍵}¨'Record.aplc' 'Producer.aplc' 'Consumer.aplc'
      #.Init Lib
      ⍙ready←1
    ∇

    ∇ p←Producer brokers;cfg
    ⍝ A producer connected to brokers (e.g. 'apl-kafka:19092')
      Init
      cfg←0 2⍴⍬
      cfg⍪←'bootstrap.servers'brokers
      cfg⍪←'client.id' 'apl-producer'
      p←⎕NEW #.Producer cfg
    ∇

    ∇ {r}←p Send args;topic;value;key
    ⍝ p Send topic value [key]
    ⍝ Messages with the same key always go to the same partition, so they
    ⍝ stay in order relative to each other.
      (topic value key)←3↑args,(≢args)↓'' '' ''
      r←p.produce topic(Encode value)(Encode key)
      :If 0≠⊃r
          ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' 11)('Message'('Kafka.Send failed: ',⍕r))
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←{timeout}Flush p;t0;quiet;rep;ok;bad
    ⍝ Wait until delivery reports stop arriving (or timeout ms, default 10000).
    ⍝ Returns delivered failed. (Uses delivery_report directly: the library's
    ⍝ update_outstanding has a LENGTH ERROR in v0.1.117.)
      :If 0=⎕NC'timeout' ⋄ timeout←10000 ⋄ :EndIf
      t0←⎕AI[3] ⋄ quiet←⎕AI[3] ⋄ ok←bad←0
      :While (500>⎕AI[3]-quiet)∧timeout>⎕AI[3]-t0
          rep←p.delivery_report 1000
          :If (0=⊃rep)∧0<≢2⊃rep
              ok+←+/0=(2⊃rep)[;2]
              bad+←+/0≠(2⊃rep)[;2]
              quiet←⎕AI[3]
          :Else
              ⎕DL 0.05
          :EndIf
      :EndWhile
      r←ok bad
    ∇

    ∇ c←Consumer(brokers group topics);cfg
    ⍝ A consumer in consumer group `group`, subscribed to topics (one or more).
    ⍝ A new group starts at the oldest message; an existing one carries on
    ⍝ where it left off (Kafka remembers each group's position).
      Init
      cfg←0 2⍴⍬
      cfg⍪←'bootstrap.servers'brokers
      cfg⍪←'client.id' 'apl-consumer'
      cfg⍪←'group.id'group
      cfg⍪←'auto.offset.reset' 'earliest'
      ⍝ If a consumer stops without saying goodbye (Ctrl+C), Kafka waits this
      ⍝ long before giving its partitions to another one (default 45 s)
      cfg⍪←'session.timeout.ms' '10000'
      c←⎕NEW #.Consumer cfg
      {}c.subscribe topics
    ∇

    ∇ msgs←{limits}Poll c;max;wait;idle;t0;last;r;rec
    ⍝ Collect waiting messages: up to max, giving up after `wait` ms if none
    ⍝ arrive, and stopping once none have arrived for `idle` ms.
    ⍝ limits: max wait idle (default 1000 10000 1000)
      :If 0=⎕NC'limits' ⋄ limits←⍬ ⋄ :EndIf
      (max wait idle)←limits,(≢limits)↓1000 10000 1000
      msgs←⍬ ⋄ t0←⎕AI[3] ⋄ last←0
      :While max>≢msgs
          :If 0=last ⋄ :AndIf wait<⎕AI[3]-t0 ⋄ :Leave ⋄ :EndIf
          :If 0≠last ⋄ :AndIf idle<⎕AI[3]-last ⋄ :Leave ⋄ :EndIf
          r←c.consume_record
          :Select ⊃r
          :Case 0
              rec←2⊃r
              msgs,←⊂Message rec.(Topic Payload Key Partition Offset)
              last←⎕AI[3]
          :Case 1                         ⍝ nothing waiting right now
          :Else
              ⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' 11)('Message'('Kafka.Poll failed: ',⍕r))
          :EndSelect
      :EndWhile
    ∇

    ∇ m←Message(topic payload key partition offset)
    ⍝ A received message as a namespace. data is the value parsed as JSON
    ⍝ (⍬ if it isn't JSON).
      m←⎕NS ⍬
      m.(topic partition offset)←topic partition offset
      m.key←Decode key
      m.value←Decode payload
      m.data←{0::⍬ ⋄ 0 ⎕JSON ⍵}m.value
    ∇

    ⍝ Text is sent as is; other arrays as JSON. Bytes travel as chars 0-255.
    Encode←{⎕UCS'UTF-8'⎕UCS{(0=10|⎕DR ⍵)∧1≥|≡⍵:,⍵ ⋄ 1 ⎕JSON ⍵}⍵}
    Decode←{'UTF-8'⎕UCS ⎕UCS ⍵}
:EndNamespace
